                        "form": "favelles"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c6b0d4d6-8302-3112-b02f-5c5478b99d19",
                        "entry_id": "36b4ba13-a2c9-35f4-9f24-70f0908110f7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Zone de misère dans une ville, un quartier, le plus souvent au Brésil ou en Amérique du Sud."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "035cad22-77d1-4d66-bcb7-544c6aab0256",
                                "sense_id": "c6b0d4d6-8302-3112-b02f-5c5478b99d19",
                                "text": "Je vis dans une favelle, au milieu des pauvres, comme eux."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6507b842-a347-4952-ace2-1b98a51935d8",
                        "source_entry_id": "36b4ba13-a2c9-35f4-9f24-70f0908110f7",
                        "source_sense_id": "c6b0d4d6-8302-3112-b02f-5c5478b99d19",
                        "target_lang_word": "slum",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "slum",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "57d3ce5d-48b5-3e66-84f4-1c3250c565a6",
                                        "entry_id": "341dd578-63ae-3825-8d90-fbe3e3f72e0f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A dilapidated neighborhood where many people live in a state of poverty."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "derogatory"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3ce56aa-c00d-4ba3-a261-2d65d3feddba",
                                                "sense_id": "57d3ce5d-48b5-3e66-84f4-1c3250c565a6",
                                                "text": "Go to the half built-upon slums behind Battlebridge […] you will find groups of boys […] squatting in the mud, among the rubbish, the broken bricks, the dust-heaps, and the fragments of timber […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c125c96b-1680-4fe9-9f61-3b3fa3ccdb44",
                                                "sense_id": "57d3ce5d-48b5-3e66-84f4-1c3250c565a6",
                                                "text": "I saw that most of those who were spending from eight to fifteen pounds monthly had the advantage of scholarships. I had before me examples of much simpler living. I came across a fair number of poor students living more humbly than I. One of them was staying in the slums in a room at two shillings a week and living on two pence worth of cocoa and bread per meal from Lockhart's cheap Cocoa Rooms."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cef55f72-4cca-45d6-9622-441feed9b5d1",
                                                "sense_id": "57d3ce5d-48b5-3e66-84f4-1c3250c565a6",
                                                "text": "Another place where, from the aesthetic point of view, a long tunnel would have been a real blessing, is East London as viewed from the carriage window on the old Great Eastern line. Despite a vast change from crowded slums to tracts of wasteland, due to its grim wartime experience, this approach still provides a shabby and unworthy introduction to the great capital."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1425114f-68ab-4a47-badc-04fabf482691",
                                                "sense_id": "57d3ce5d-48b5-3e66-84f4-1c3250c565a6",
                                                "text": "Pearson's London was what we now call central London, and much of it was slums. Today most of us wouldn't say no to a pied à terre in Clerkenwell, but in 1850 it was a slum. Drury Lane? A slum. Seven Dials and Covent Garden? Holborn and Finsbury? Slums."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fee451fd-aadf-3bd9-b2fa-2a067604ddcc",
                                        "entry_id": "341dd578-63ae-3825-8d90-fbe3e3f72e0f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Inexpensive trinkets awarded as prizes in a carnival game."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "417adbc7-55f4-484b-99b2-8af47bd14635",
                                                "sense_id": "fee451fd-aadf-3bd9-b2fa-2a067604ddcc",
                                                "text": "The lower the price of slum the better it is for the operator who can either give more of it out or build up the size of his big prizes. It is the big prizes that bring the play, even though the winner has to be satisfied with a piece of slum for his efforts."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "592661d3-610c-4abc-9d5e-56efb40c828f",
                                                "sense_id": "fee451fd-aadf-3bd9-b2fa-2a067604ddcc",
                                                "text": "Another hanky pank is the darts and balloons. No gaffs, no grift, nothing phoney. Game for the kids and the family. Get a dozen gross of slum and pass it out to the kids, and everybody'll love you."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9c79933-eb98-4ec4-9e9f-66c943dd8e56",
                                                "sense_id": "fee451fd-aadf-3bd9-b2fa-2a067604ddcc",
                                                "text": "Making twenty times his investment in only seconds, the concessionaire smiled as he awarded the nickel slum, often a stuffed worm, to each unwitting pigeon."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "slum",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0b0b1410-7bbd-3aef-9020-ec522451efb3",
                                        "entry_id": "ca889ac2-4917-38ce-8da6-6eaa503fa15e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To visit a neighborhood of a status below one's own."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e2adb9c9-1dbb-4340-a2c0-f2ace8ab78b3",
                                                "sense_id": "0b0b1410-7bbd-3aef-9020-ec522451efb3",
                                                "text": "When you meet the girl who wouldn't et cetera you will tell her that you are slumming, visiting your own six A.M. Lower East Side of the soul on a lark, stepping nimbly between the piles of garbage to the gay marimba rhythms in your head."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4bac50cc-62fd-402d-a133-1fa95239fc6b",
                                                "sense_id": "0b0b1410-7bbd-3aef-9020-ec522451efb3",
                                                "text": "While slumming had long been an indulgence; if not liberty, of many well-to-do men (and some women), the intimate theaters created by Prohibition brought together elements of normally disparate social groups through a special form of bonding, breaking the law and enjoying it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7fdde1d6-acee-38ce-af50-81dd9e7badc4",
                                        "entry_id": "ca889ac2-4917-38ce-8da6-6eaa503fa15e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To saunter about in a disreputable manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "dated",
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "slum",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "14055808-3d10-39d2-9e31-3f1b223690f0",
                                        "entry_id": "8f1c4472-26cd-3036-8631-e04e5b6d26bc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Slumgullion; a meat-based stew."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "slum",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e7177e5e-98b3-3fd0-a817-71797a97a52f",
                                        "entry_id": "44d2db56-e3cc-37fb-ada7-8882023e9807",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Nonsense; humbug."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "slang",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "42c93aff-e5b5-4fac-ade6-db5b2a189b3c",
                                                "sense_id": "e7177e5e-98b3-3fd0-a817-71797a97a52f",
                                                "text": "And this, without more slum began, / Over a flowing pot-house can, / To settle, without botheration, / The rigs of this here tip-top nation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d13d3609-aa71-4b8a-8084-c9752d5fc27b",
                        "source_entry_id": "36b4ba13-a2c9-35f4-9f24-70f0908110f7",
                        "source_sense_id": "c6b0d4d6-8302-3112-b02f-5c5478b99d19",
                        "target_lang_word": "shantytown",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "shantytown",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2a10f8fb-795b-3fcd-954e-48e9e694af87",
                                        "entry_id": "87e2cc41-e2ab-3324-9995-c4baeb932438",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An area containing a collection of shacks, shanties or makeshift dwellings."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac8bbb97-d9ef-4ab4-998d-c81edcd430c1",
                                                "sense_id": "2a10f8fb-795b-3fcd-954e-48e9e694af87",
                                                "text": "The forest gave way to shantytowns that stitched themselves into waves of blue-tented internally displaced camps and then stone dwellings hundreds of years old."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4f12b277-6be8-46b6-8a78-87f431359820",
                        "source_entry_id": "36b4ba13-a2c9-35f4-9f24-70f0908110f7",
                        "source_sense_id": "c6b0d4d6-8302-3112-b02f-5c5478b99d19",
                        "target_lang_word": "ghetto",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ghetto",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "26a7870f-73b3-3a53-b648-c09475a9936f",
                                        "entry_id": "ae5559d3-b645-3190-9043-af458e9d6703",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An (often walled) area of a city in which Jews are concentrated by force and law. (Used particularly of areas in medieval Italy and in Nazi-controlled Europe.)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8dc26e90-ec28-4517-97f7-34dedc034a50",
                                                "sense_id": "26a7870f-73b3-3a53-b648-c09475a9936f",
                                                "text": "The Venetian ghetto, according to Sennett, was to provide protection from the unclean bodies of the Jews and their sullying touch. The Roman ghetto, on the other hand, was planned as an area for mission. It was supposed to collect the Jews in one place, so that it would be easier to convert them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8f1825a-bd89-489c-8734-7f24704670be",
                                                "sense_id": "26a7870f-73b3-3a53-b648-c09475a9936f",
                                                "text": "[…] concentrating the Jewish community into ghettoes. The Germans not only started the ghettoes, but they had also opened a concentration camp […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f23e4e6b-ee7e-4fa1-b5cf-bcab5ccb7d17",
                                                "sense_id": "26a7870f-73b3-3a53-b648-c09475a9936f",
                                                "text": "Established by the Germans in October 1940, the Warsaw Ghetto was the largest Jewish ghetto in German-occupied Europe."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fff903f1-7aaa-368c-a354-b32f821b0a70",
                                        "entry_id": "ae5559d3-b645-3190-9043-af458e9d6703",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An (often impoverished) area of a city inhabited predominantly by members of a specific nationality, ethnicity, or race."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c559232-c943-43d6-851f-8d0eb6f12181",
                                                "sense_id": "fff903f1-7aaa-368c-a354-b32f821b0a70",
                                                "text": "Charlestown would also become one of Boston's three large Irish ghettoes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3fcdeabe-2094-45c1-a3d1-aa8cc40883f8",
                                                "sense_id": "fff903f1-7aaa-368c-a354-b32f821b0a70",
                                                "text": "By 1960 the growth and development of Chicago's black areas of residence confirmed the existence of the city's second ghetto."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fd2e772c-5b45-3343-80c9-36194aa88b27",
                                        "entry_id": "ae5559d3-b645-3190-9043-af458e9d6703",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An area in which people who are distinguished by sharing something other than ethnicity concentrate or are concentrated."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f9c0486-d3f5-4893-85d9-88f2112741ba",
                                                "sense_id": "fd2e772c-5b45-3343-80c9-36194aa88b27",
                                                "text": "Counterhegemonic spaces imagined as bounded territories ensure that heteronormativity is fixed beyond the borders of the gay ghetto. The rural and suburban lives of lesbian and gay people are made invisible and signified as inauthentic."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e33018ba-4a3c-490b-9f6f-f8974a7dc0d6",
                                                "sense_id": "fd2e772c-5b45-3343-80c9-36194aa88b27",
                                                "text": "The student ghetto, southwest of the centre, is inside the triangle formed by [three streets] and is full of open-air bars, internet cafés, fast-food shops — and students."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3409fa2-265c-4e22-977e-d10499628387",
                                                "sense_id": "fd2e772c-5b45-3343-80c9-36194aa88b27",
                                                "text": "They're back in the student ghetto now, on oak-shaded streets lined with run-down houses filled with nonnuclear families of all varieties and kinds. Safe now from the tractor beams of the horrible good Christians, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e2a01cee-eb4c-3b20-b3a1-fd4001103f6d",
                                        "entry_id": "ae5559d3-b645-3190-9043-af458e9d6703",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An isolated, self-contained, segregated subsection, area or field of interest; often of minority or specialist interest."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "sometimes"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9453f65e-c3b9-408c-85be-0540311a5f1f",
                                                "sense_id": "e2a01cee-eb4c-3b20-b3a1-fd4001103f6d",
                                                "text": "Abraham Merritt wrote for the pulps and never in his lifetime achieved critical success. Yet he had a devoted following in the science fiction ghetto who admired the clarity of his style and his power to evoke moods."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5a9a0e3-8468-49c4-86ae-6e593a8e9162",
                                                "sense_id": "e2a01cee-eb4c-3b20-b3a1-fd4001103f6d",
                                                "text": "Invent is undoubtedly the wrong word, but the push from government was crucial in getting the Internet out of its academic ghetto."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "631b67c9-b7f4-4b02-bf9e-b14e88ac797b",
                                                "sense_id": "e2a01cee-eb4c-3b20-b3a1-fd4001103f6d",
                                                "text": "2016 January 10, Quentin Tarantino, 73rd Golden Globe Awards\nEnnio Morricone... is my favourite composer - and when I say favourite composer, I don't mean movie composer - that ghetto. I'm talking about Mozart, I'm talking about Beethoven, I'm talking about Schubert. That's who I'm talking about."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "ghetto",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7fb03f9f-dabc-3532-bcf2-ab8e65dfb35e",
                                        "entry_id": "dfd23cac-ceff-349a-a032-b06b81dd7379",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or relating to a ghetto or to ghettos in general."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1af9dfa-c7d7-450c-b074-7e26b442e813",
                                                "sense_id": "7fb03f9f-dabc-3532-bcf2-ab8e65dfb35e",
                                                "text": "Those residing in ghetto communities were particularly ill equipped to adapt to the seismic changes taking place in the U.S. economy; they were left isolated and jobless."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f47145d6-2b13-3c1f-896a-d817ac062dcd",
                                        "entry_id": "dfd23cac-ceff-349a-a032-b06b81dd7379",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Unseemly and indecorous or of low quality; cheap; shabby, crude."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c7060b0e-899a-4775-9fc7-fe4c9d6b4ab1",
                                                "sense_id": "f47145d6-2b13-3c1f-896a-d817ac062dcd",
                                                "text": "My apartment's so ghetto, the rats and cockroaches filed a complaint with the city!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "caf63616-0cfa-4f45-86ce-a1d7bf064b32",
                                                "sense_id": "f47145d6-2b13-3c1f-896a-d817ac062dcd",
                                                "text": "I like to drive ghetto cars; if they break down you can just abandon them and pick up a new one!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "02052bf1-ff44-427a-8cdf-45dd6c9dfe31",
                                                "sense_id": "f47145d6-2b13-3c1f-896a-d817ac062dcd",
                                                "text": "I had not used very many minutes on my phone. Here we pay for our minutes prior to using them, and it gets expensive. I did not want her using up all my minutes. That was very ghetto and disrespectful."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b8efa69-7c11-406c-88b7-966241efb5dc",
                                                "sense_id": "f47145d6-2b13-3c1f-896a-d817ac062dcd",
                                                "text": "In some kind of warped hometown loyalty, sometime during the conversation folks would stake their claim to owning the bottom. Philly is more ghetto than D.C. Or is it that DC. is more ghetto than Philly? Or Dallas (LA) is more ghetto than LA."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa219141-eaa3-4aac-9700-9e61083e6d44",
                                                "sense_id": "f47145d6-2b13-3c1f-896a-d817ac062dcd",
                                                "text": "One guest did not pay. One of my checks remained open. They bolted and hit the service door. A walkout. Very ghetto."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "144224cd-97e0-42de-b7a9-d4b287887392",
                                                "sense_id": "f47145d6-2b13-3c1f-896a-d817ac062dcd",
                                                "text": "It was like an awesome trip walking though the old house on Douglas, a lot had changed and my dad had it looking more ghetto than ever. He had a dog that he was watching while a buddy of his was in prison. It was a female Rottweiler"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "39fd5b4f-64b2-3a7a-a3fb-fd74de984b3e",
                                        "entry_id": "dfd23cac-ceff-349a-a032-b06b81dd7379",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Characteristic of the style, speech, or behavior of residents of a predominantly black or other ghetto in the United States."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "informal",
                                            "offensive",
                                            "often"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8cfa2b17-179f-46ef-991c-c0593b02575e",
                                                "sense_id": "39fd5b4f-64b2-3a7a-a3fb-fd74de984b3e",
                                                "text": "The music I liked was very ghetto and gritty. It was the stuff that didn't really cross over much, but spoke to a roots black experience. People don't understand this now, but the falsetto, crying singers were the most ghetto back then."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ce57a5a-97d8-4c67-8d6b-12330cc469ed",
                                                "sense_id": "39fd5b4f-64b2-3a7a-a3fb-fd74de984b3e",
                                                "text": "You're the one that grew up in the suburbs and you act way more ghetto than I do.” “I am not ghetto.” Val said in an English accent and broke out laughing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7bb1297-ded6-44a8-a5bc-5501c2bae8c6",
                                                "sense_id": "39fd5b4f-64b2-3a7a-a3fb-fd74de984b3e",
                                                "text": "I beat up my kid's principal. Can you get any more ghetto than that?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eedd4d9b-c02e-472b-917c-7bba38188b1e",
                                                "sense_id": "39fd5b4f-64b2-3a7a-a3fb-fd74de984b3e",
                                                "text": "He wasn't lying because, truth be told, I looked a lot like Halle Berry, only I was much thicker in all the right places and I was way more ghetto than Halle. And I had the tattoos and the attitude to match."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7928fd77-ec1b-439f-881f-5e10118f471a",
                                                "sense_id": "39fd5b4f-64b2-3a7a-a3fb-fd74de984b3e",
                                                "text": "Oh yeah, we played the whole thing, I mean we was acting more ghetto than what we was. We was talking slangs and giving dabs every time we said so"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "10c184d6-460d-414c-b442-2fe9fb2c6270",
                                                "sense_id": "39fd5b4f-64b2-3a7a-a3fb-fd74de984b3e",
                                                "text": "Kesha rang us up, and instructed another girl in the back to add extra food to the bag. \"Your girl is kinda ghetto ain't she?\" I asked when we left the store. \"No more ghetto than anyone else around here\" he replied,"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a4ea8afc-f4c4-3780-bdc5-ab60f98e8761",
                                        "entry_id": "dfd23cac-ceff-349a-a032-b06b81dd7379",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having been raised in a ghetto in the United States."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "ghetto",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5122f311-e41f-3549-8ce0-843874725481",
                                        "entry_id": "b40f996d-df67-3050-bc98-cf191641ca7d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To confine (a specified group of people) to a ghetto."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1497507f-ec56-4f1e-8ab7-5efaefe47521",
                                                "sense_id": "5122f311-e41f-3549-8ce0-843874725481",
                                                "text": "This is, in brief, a part of the story of the ghettoing of a large segment of Denver's Negro population."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "56fb80e8-0b8f-4104-95e9-7abb69c4567b",
                                                "sense_id": "5122f311-e41f-3549-8ce0-843874725481",
                                                "text": "All African states practised racist policies. In the 1950s and 1960s, Egypt, Libya, Algeria, Morocco and Tunisia expelled more than a quarter of a million Jews and ghettoed the few thousand who remained. In the 1960s the United Republic of Tanzania expelled its Arabs or deprived them of equal rights."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
